  A2 closes IFF   path(G) >= path(G') + h   ... call it (A2-PATH).
  Given F11 on G' (path(G') >= rad(G') + 4) and the inequality proved above,
  (A2-PATH) yields  path(G) >= rad(G') + 4 + h >= rad(G) + 4,  which is Problem A.

  (A2-PATH) IS NOT PROVED HERE AND IS NOT CLAIMED.  Two warnings the prompt already
  carries and that any attempt must respect:
    * a 'hair' can be a TRIANGLE-LEAF CHAIN, not only a bare pendant path -- PART 0
      exhibits a triangle whose vertex has a = 1, so peeling can bite into a triangle;
    * the peeled material must be converted into h extra INDUCED-path vertices
      attached to a path OF G', and inducedness across the join is the hard part:
      a hair vertex may be adjacent to several vertices of the G'-path.
  RULING DB is NOT invoked: (A2-PATH) has not been through the hand-computability
  filter and this round does not put it through.

